WEBVTT

NOTE Sentence timings are approximate, not word-aligned.

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.100
Pooling memory can make a larger model seem possible.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.830
Here, ideal four-bit weights take about thirty-three
gibibytes.

3
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:15.437
Add our assumed overhead, cache, and workspace, and the
total rises to about forty-four.

4
00:00:16.087 --> 00:00:21.538
At twelve usable gibibytes per pool, that means at least
four pools in aggregate.

5
00:00:21.538 --> 00:00:27.393
But adding their capacities doesn't prove the model can
actually be placed across them.

6
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.597
Speed needs a separate calculation.

7
00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:36.046
In this one-token serial example, every stage depends on
the previous one.

8
00:00:36.046 --> 00:00:43.999
With the stated link assumptions, sixteen stages spend
about four tenths of a second on communication alone.

9
00:00:44.653 --> 00:00:51.214
That gives an optimistic communication-only ceiling of
about two and a half tokens per second.

10
00:00:51.214 --> 00:00:58.264
These are assumptions, not household measurements, and
other execution graphs need separate analysis.
